# Turath — Project Conventions

Next.js web for **Turath (تراث)**: Syria tourism, heritage, and hospitality.
Not Flutter. Not NestJS. UI is custom glassmorphism — no component kit.

**Every pass:** read `docs/PAGES.md` before adding or changing routes, layouts, or nav.
Do not invent pages. If a route changes, update `docs/PAGES.md` first.
UI copy in `messages/` stays user-friendly even when `PAGES.md` uses a different domain name.
Admin URLs: `config/adminRoutes.ts` — do not hardcode `/admin/...` slugs.

## Domain

Multi-tenant platform: tourists discover heritage + book hotels, restaurants, trips,
events, and guides (cash on arrival). Providers run inventory and check-in.
Super admin vets KYC, CMS, commissions. Web shows QR + backup code; camera scan is Flutter.

Mock roles now: `TOURIST` | `PROVIDER_STAFF` | `PROVIDER_OWNER` | `SUPER_ADMIN`.
Real JWT/RBAC only when the API exists — do not build a permission engine first.

## Stack

- Next.js 16 App Router + React 19 + TypeScript
- Tailwind CSS v4 — no MUI, Emotion, styled-components, shadcn, Radix, Headless UI
- `next-intl` — i18n/RTL. Messages in `messages/{locale}.json` (en + ar only)
- `zustand` — client state (auth mock, sidebar, filters, toasts). No React Context
  for global state. No Redux.
- `fetch` + `@tanstack/react-query` — every API call. No axios. No `useEffect` +
  `useState` fetch flags. Server data lives in Query, never duplicated in zustand
- `react-hook-form` + `zod` + `@hookform/resolvers` — every form. One zod file per
  domain in `lib/validation/`
- `next-themes` — light/dark (class strategy). Not a second theme store in zustand
- `date-fns` — the only date library (no moment, no dayjs)
- `lucide-react` — icons. Custom SVG only if lucide cannot provide it
- `clsx` + `tailwind-merge` — className composition
- `next/font` — English matches the lockup serif (Playfair Display). Arabic matches the lockup Naskh (Cairo).
  No Google Fonts CDN in CSS. No `@fontsource`

- `framer-motion` — client-only motion (viewport reveals, layout transitions,
  drag reels, springs). Shared variants live in `lib/motion/variants.ts`.
  Server Components stay motion-free; isolate `motion.*` usage behind a
  `'use client'` leaf component.

When those pages exist: `maplibre-gl` for `/explore` (not Google/Mapbox);
`qrcode.react` for vouchers; `nuqs` for search URL state.

Do not add: axios, Redux, JWT client libs, Stripe, Firebase,
socket.io, chart kits until admin analytics is real, any UI component package
(`react-select`, `react-table`, `react-switch`, etc.).

## No UI libraries — build our own

Every primitive (Button, Input, Select, Table, Modal, Tabs, Tooltip, Dropdown,
DatePicker, GlassPanel, EmptyState, ErrorState, PageHeader, Logo) lives in
`components/ui/`, Tailwind only. Check `components/ui/` before adding a new one.

## Typography

Exposed as tokens in `app/globals.css`: `--font-heading` → `font-heading` (h1–h6
default) and `--font-sans` → `font-sans` (body). Never hardcode `font-family`
in a component. Arabic needs ~+25% line-height vs Latin (set on `html[lang="ar"]`).

## Colors & tokens

All colors, gradients, and glass surfaces are CSS variables in `app/globals.css`
(light and dark). Tailwind theme maps to those variables. Never hardcode hex/rgb
in a component — use tokens (`bg-app`, `text-prose`, `border-glass`, `bg-glass`, …).
New color from design → add the token first, then use it.

## Glass UI

Tailwind only, no glass library. Reuse `GlassPanel` / tokens, do not paste
`backdrop-blur-xl bg-white/10 border border-white/15` on every card.
Typical: frost, 1px light border, large radius (~20–32px), soft shadow.

## Light / dark

Support both from the start. `next-themes` + Tailwind `dark:`. Every new
component must look correct in both modes. `Logo` switches assets by theme
(see logos below). Never ship a one-mode-only component.

## Logos (`public/`)

- Light full lockup → `/main-logo.png`
- Dark full lockup → `/dark-main-logo.png`
- Light compact / collapsed sidebar → `/simple-logo.png`
- Dark compact → `/dark-simple-logo.png`
- Favicon / PWA only → `/app-logo.png`
- Receipts / invoices / vouchers only → `/reciept-logo.png` (keep this filename)

Never put a light logo on a dark surface or the reverse.

## Internationalization — en / ar

Every new UI string goes in **both** `messages/en.json` and `messages/ar.json`
from the start. Never hardcode user-facing text. Never leave Arabic for later.

RTL/LTR from day one: logical Tailwind (`ps-`, `pe-`, `ms-`, `me-`, `start-`,
`end-`), never physical `left`/`right` for direction-sensitive layout.
Verify both directions. `html` `lang` + `dir` come from `next-intl`.

Money: display `150,000 SYP (~$10.50)` via a shared formatter. Amounts are SYP.

## Layouts & page headers

Pages do not rebuild chrome. `(auth)` uses `AuthLayout` from `app/(auth)/layout.tsx`.
`(public)` / `(user)` / `(provider)` / `(admin)` each have their own shell in
`components/layout/` (header/sidebar + content), wired in that route group's
`layout.tsx`. `(user)`, `(provider)`, and `(admin)` shells gate on
`isAuthenticated` plus the matching role. Never one sidebar with all
roles. Staff nav hides owner-only items even with mock auth.

Titles/breadcrumbs/actions: `config/pageHeaders.ts` + shared `PageHeader`.
Nav: `config/nav.ts` with `roles` arrays. Pages do not hardcode header markup.

## Error, loaders, empty

Every data view must handle Query states: loading (shared skeleton), error
(shared `ErrorState` + retry), empty (shared `EmptyState`). Build once in
`components/ui/`. No one-off loaders per page.

## Performance

- Query `staleTime` / `gcTime` — Query is source of truth for server data
- Next.js `dynamic()` for heavy maps / QR
- Memoize only where re-renders are costly
- No duplicate libraries for the same job
- Tree-shake lucide imports

## Code cleanliness

Follow `.cursor/rules/turath-quality.mdc`. Senior-level, typed, no dead code.

## Folder structure

```
app/
  (auth)/                 # login, register, otp, password
  (public)/               # tourist discovery, booking
  (user)/                 # signed-in user area: /user dashboard, bookings, saved, profile (UserShell)
  (provider)/
  (admin)/
  layout.tsx
  globals.css             # Tailwind + design tokens
components/
  ui/                     # Button, Input, GlassPanel, Modal, EmptyState...
  layout/                 # AuthLayout, PublicShell, UserShell, ProviderShell, AdminShell
  logo/
config/
  nav.ts
  pageHeaders.ts
  adminRoutes.ts
lib/
  api/client.ts           # fetch wrapper
  auth/session.ts         # mock session now; JWT later
  format/                 # money, dates
  validation/             # zod schemas
  motion/                 # shared framer-motion variants
  mock/                   # static mock content until the API exists
hooks/
services/                 # one file per REST resource
store/                    # zustand stores
messages/
  en.json
  ar.json
public/                   # logos only as specified
docs/PAGES.md
```

## Conventions

- Stick to this folder structure. Do not invent parallel homes for services,
  stores, or UI primitives.
- One service file per REST resource in `services/`. Pages/hooks call services,
  never `fetch` directly.
- One zustand store per concern (`authStore`, `uiStore`, `toastStore`, …).
- Types live next to the domain (`*.types.ts` or in the service), not one
  giant global types file.
- Prefer extending `components/ui/` over a new npm UI dependency.
- Mock API/data is fine until NestJS exists; still go through services + Query.
